  "description": "Florida's 16th Congressional District will elect a new representative in 2026 following the retirement of incumbent Republican Vern Buchanan, who has held the seat since 2007. The district covers all of Manatee County and portions of southern Hillsborough County, including Bradenton, Sarasota, and parts of the Tampa Bay area. The seat has become reliably Republican in recent cycles, with Buchanan winning 59.5% in 2024. The open-seat race has attracted a crowded field of candidates from both major parties, with the Republican primary expected to be highly competitive given the district's lean. The Democratic primary features several candidates with military, education, and legal backgrounds. The general election will test whether the district's Republican tilt holds in a midterm environment.",
